\nProgramme\nEssential skills training\nFieldwork\nChallenge Teams\nProject List 2025-26\nProject List 2024-25\nProject List 2023-24\nProject List 2022-23\nProject List 2021-22\nProject List 2020-21\nProject List 2019-20\nProject List 2018-19\nProject List 2017-18\nProject List 2016-17\nProject List 2015-16\nResearch\nEquity, Diversity and Inclusion\nInstitute EDI activities\nIn this section\nScience and Solutions for a Changing Planet DTP\nOur students\nOur team\nProgramme\nResearch\nEquity, Diversity and Inclusion\nScience and Solutions for a Changing Planet DTP\nImperial Home\nGrantham Institute \u2013 Climate Change and the Environment\nEducation and training\nScience and Solutions for a Changing Planet DTP\nScience and Solutions for a Changing Planet DTP\nEducation and training\nOur students\nOur team\nProgramme\nResearch\nEquity, Diversity and Inclusion\n**Please note that the SSCP DTP welcomed its last cohort in October 2024. These pages are no longer being updated.\nYou can learn more about postgraduate research at the Grantham Institute here.**\nThe Science and Solutions for a Changing Planet Doctoral Training Partnership (SSCP DTP) is a NERC-funded doctoral training programme led by Imperial College London. It has been hosted by the Grantham Institute, working with six core partners and over 20 Imperial Departments since 2014. The SSCP DTP has brought together and trained a new generation of environmental experts and leaders to tackle some of the toughest challenges of our time.\nThe SSCP DTP welcomed its final student cohort in autumn 2024. The Grantham Institute hosts a large and vibrant network of active PhDs and PhD alumni.\nCurrent PhD opportunities at the Grantham Institute are listed here and the full range of Grantham Institute education courses and trainings can be found here.\nWho are we?\nOur students\nMeet the cohorts of the SSCP DTP.\nOur team\nFind out about our staff and directors, student reps and core partners.\nOur programme\nFind out abo